From 1d3082a8272621de3a1db989158881b4790510d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bluelightsaber <26096600+bluelightsaber@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:17:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 40/51] soc: mediatek: mt6797: GPS character devices on ConSys

Add /dev/stpgps (raw STP task 2, WMT GPS function on open, optional LNA
GPIO) and the /dev/gps mailbox expected by the MediaTek location daemon.
WMT clients may now claim the GPS task; ConSys has no VCN33 rail for it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/Kconfig         |   8 +
 drivers/soc/mediatek/Makefile        |   1 +
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-consys.c |   8 +
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-gps.c    | 415 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-wmt.c    |  10 +-
 include/linux/mt6797-consys.h        |   1 +
 6 files changed, 439 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-gps.c

